  "part_3_demand": {
    "threshold": "a disclosed modeling threshold, not a mathematical derivation: a (city, candidate) cell is meaningful when its calibration-sample demand is at least 1% of that city's calibration-sample orders. 1% sits below every deliberately designed stress-scenario share in methodology section 8.2, the smallest being tight_low_budget at 3%, so it cannot be met by absorbing an intentional stress category. cells below it are rare residuals, accepted as stress conditions, consistent with section 2's deliberately difficult conditions",
    "overlap_convention": "an order counts toward every candidate domain that contains its weight when demand per (city, candidate) is tabulated and the 1% threshold is applied: meaningfulness belongs to a domain, and picking one domain for an order before any agent holds one would be an arbitrary attribution. the objective counts orders, not cells: an order is in scope once if any of its domains is meaningful in its city, and covered once if any eligible provider can carry it, so overlapping domains never count the same order twice and a domain boundary such as exactly 1000 kg is judged by the order's exact weight, not by whole-cell containment. the cell-summed alternative, which would count an order once per meaningful domain containing it, is scored for every assignment as a sensitivity",
